graph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ°And Simeon blessed them, and said unto Mary his mother, Behold, this child is set for the fall and rising again of many in Israel; and for a sign which shall be spoken against;¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙh(yea, a sword shall pierce through thy own soul also,) that the thoughts of many hearts may be revealed.¦layout ªlast_verse#…¤book)§chapter«first_verse$ªlast_verse&¦verses“„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙªAnd there was one Anna, a prophetess, the daughter of Phanuel, of the tribe of Aser: she was of a great age, and had lived with an husband seven years from her virginity;¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’and she was a widow of about fourscore and four years, which departed not from the temple, but served God with fastings and prayers night and day.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙˆAnd she coming in that instant gave thanks likewise unto the Lord, and spake of him to all them that looked for redemption in Jerusalem.¦layout ªlast_verse&…¤book)§chapter«first_verse'ªlast_verse(¦verses’„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€And when they had performed all things according to the law of the Lord, they returned into Galilee, to their own city Nazareth.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙfAnd the child grew, and waxed strong in spirit, filled with wisdom: and the grace of God was upon him.¦layout ªlast_verse(…¤book)§chapter«first_verse)ªlast_verse2¦versesš„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙJNow his parents went to Jerusalem every year at the feast of the passover.¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZAnd when he was twelve years old, they went up to Jerusalem after the custom of the feast.¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd when they had fulfilled the days, as they returned, the child Jesus tarried behind in Jerusalem; and Joseph and his mother knew not of it.¦layout ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ…But they, supposing him to have been in the company, went a day's journey; and they sought him among their kinsfolk and acquaintance.¦layout ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNAnd when they found him not, they turned back again to Jerusalem, seeking him.¦layout ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ›And it came to pass, that after three days they found him in the temple, sitting in the midst of the doctors, both hearing them, and asking them questions.¦layout ªlast_verse.„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHAnd all that heard him were astonished at his understanding and answers.¦layout ªlast_verse/„¥verse0¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¢And when they saw him, they were amazed: and his mother said unto him, Son, why hast thou thus dealt with us? behold, thy father and I have sought thee sorrowing.¦layout ªlast_verse0„¥verse1¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjAnd he said unto them, How is it that ye sought me? wist ye not that I must be about my Father's business?¦layout ªlast_verse1„¥verse2¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ<And they understood not the saying which he spake unto them.¦layout ªlast_verse2…¤book)§chapter«first_verse3ªlast_verse4¦verses’„¥verse3¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€And he went down with them, and came to Nazareth, and was subject unto them: but his mother kept all these sayings in her heart.¦layout ªlast_verse3„¥verse4¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙJAnd Jesus increased in wisdom and stature, and in favour with God and man.¦layout ªlast_verse4